# 15. Optical Alignment

Proper alignment is essential.

Verify:

- Lens centered above display.
- Glass positioned at ~45°.
- Display parallel to lens.
- Reflection centered.
- Avatar appears in the middle of the viewing area.

---

# 16. Calibration

## Step 1

Power on the display.

---

## Step 2

Display calibration image.

---

## Step 3

Adjust lens height until image is sharp.

---

## Step 4

Adjust reflective glass angle until the floating image appears centered.

---

## Step 5

Verify viewing from different angles.

---

## Step 6

Lock all optical components in place.

